# GD-2 (round 19): L §3.1 `monthday`: "A day of the year without its year (13 April). `02-29` is no month-day ...
# (refused, `LOAD-PARSE`). Month-days compare with `==` and `!=` only; any order or arithmetic on them is refused (§8.4)."
# L §4.2: "A day a source fixes in every year is an input of that type, with rows (`fam1_file_by = 04-30`) and pins
# (`with fam1_file_by = 05-31`) like any other, and `day_of(y, fam1_file_by)` is that day in year y"; day_of(y, md)
# "the day of month-day md (§3.1) in year y, y a year value or a key of a year index": due[2026] = 2026-04-30,
# due[2027] = 2027-04-30; under the pin 05-31, due[2026] = 2026-05-31. The month-day prints as written.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2026..2027
input file_by: monthday
input other: monthday
def due[y in yrs]: date = day_of(y, file_by)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  file_by = 04-30
  other = 04-30

ask q: due[2026], due[2027], file_by
ask p: due[2026] with file_by = 05-31
=== expect
p: 2026-05-31
  pinned: file_by = 05-31
  cut 2026-12-31
q: (2026-04-30, 2027-04-30, 04-30)
  cut 2026-12-31
